# parse/lword (id 68): word lexer (names, functions, booleans, A1 references, A1:B2, A:C, 1:5 ranges).
# Per char: KEY X0 (base 39: A..Z 1..26, 0..9 27..36, '.' 37, up to 10 chars), KLEN X1 (100 = has
# '$' '_' ':'), COL X2, ROW X3, RS X4 (reference pattern: 0 start, 1 after $, 2 letters, 3 after row $,
# 4 digits, 5 not a reference, 6 row digits with no letters), FLAGS X5 (row abs + 2 col abs; in the
# row-digits state the '$' value 2 means row absolute), OPND1 X6 (packed first corner), CSn X7 (colon
# seen: 1 cell corner, 2 column corner, 3 row corner). ':' after a valid corner starts the second one.
# '!' after a plain word (TV >= 0, no '$', no colon) -> shpack 121 PC 0 (sheet prefix, chars TV..I-1).
# Any other char ends the word: TK = [char is '('], next 69 (wordend). Note: weights/parse/lword.md
